==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|vinr}}, {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*winiz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*wenh₁-||to seek, desire, love, win}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈvɪːnʏr/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|ɪːnʏr|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|vinar|vinir}}

# a [[friend]]{{jump|is|friend|d|s}}
#: {{ux|is|Þú ert '''vinur''' minn.|You are my '''friend'''.}}
#: {{ux|is|Þú ert góður '''vinur'''.|You are a good '''friend'''.}}
# {{context|colloquial|slang|often used with a definite article|lang=is}} [[mate]], [[lad]], an affectionate moniker for a close [[friend]] or [[pal]], especially used as a form of [[address]]{{jump|is|mate|s}}
#: {{ux|is|[[jæja|Jæja]] '''vinurinn''', ætli maður fari ekki að [[koma sér af stað]].|Well '''mate''', I guess we should [[get going]].}}

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-m-s3|v|i|n|i=?i}}

